{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: independent review of the residual scale-envelope evidence delivery at exact head cbc3b81bd77424e6b141856264af7432c8a3c4f4 on request/scale-envelope-evidence (pushed; two commits over main 9fbc913e; seventeen changed paths; clean merge onto current main). Governing request: 0b5fdd93 (#20084, planner's recovery of the residual #7454 scale-envelope outcome) under my promise 35715472; start check and measurement-window asserts rest on that promise. Two commits by design: 0b689fe2 is the harness head at which the campaign ran and must stay the measured revision (harness_commit and candidate_commit in the retained evidence), and cbc3b81bd77424e6b141856264af7432c8a3c4f4 adds the retained run and the pages. The reporting artifact is git:sha1:84ecd0f16c8efa6bb6abe3d106d348d2c4fd8549 at docs/reference/performance.md, published last on the promise; the companions are the harness sources and tests in cmd/gitseq-perf, internal/perflane and internal/perfscenario, performance/contract-v3.json, the five retained files under performance/retained/envelope-20260909-0b689fe2 (evidence, samples, bench lines, the campaign load log and the pre-registered classification rules), performance/README.md and docs/reference/limits.md. What the head delivers: a bounded envelope tier under contract-v3 (v2 byte-identical, its digest unmoved), joint actor cells and a checkpoint-bytes metric read in the lane parent after the worker exits; one campaign of ten cases with two primary samples and one diagnostic each, every digest equal, load 2.67 to 4.40 with 3 to 4 of background; the versioned PREVIEW and FIRST-PRODUCTION target table with planning, measured and governing tags and reasons; the five residual dimensions classified measured; the 500,000 checkpoint restart at 69.3 to 69.4 s stated as a miss against the historical, unadopted 60 s figure (improved from 72.986 s); full-verification memory at 15.1 to 17.7 GiB stated as a measured fact outside the adopted resident-memory outcome with no target, neither pass nor miss; the four existing lanes preserved verbatim with one false status sentence corrected from the fold; limits.md distinguishing refusals from measured envelopes. Things to check: A, every number on the pages traces to samples.jsonl or evidence.json (the load log and the classification rules are retained beside the run; the review request also attaches the run summary and the prep and chain logs); B, no pass is claimed against an unadopted target and no target was weakened; C, the harness change leaves every contract-v2 tier byte-identical, the checkpoint-bytes read cannot perturb a sample, failRun cannot mask a cause, compare mode still builds a base worker from main (gate attached); D, the four preserved lanes and the smoke-baseline rows are unchanged in every number; E, request conditions 1 to 5. Known and deliberately left: performance.md and performance/HEAD-WAIT.md disagree on one published head-wait figure (28 versus 29 ref reads for eight idle waiters), unchanged here because fixing it restates a published number and belongs to its own decision; #7454's wording asked to publish the historical restart figures unchanged, which conflicts with this request's rule that a historical measurement is not a current-head result, so both are cited as history and re-measured; six of the ten cases carry a correctness digest that equals the trusted digest by construction (status responses), so the page does not repeat the memory lane's stronger-sounding wording for them. Follow-through after your verdict: I will file one bounded implementation child for the 500,000 restart miss resting on the retained-evidence artifact, ratify, merge with exact-path succession (all in-target predecessors at the changed paths are my own; codex's directory pointers are wider and carried; two outside-target candidates of mine at 61b33f37 and 2cb7117f will be sealed abandoned and retired), push, check CI and remove the worktree. Please record Architecture (performance harness and evidence layer; contract-v3 is a new versioned workload contract beside v2; no kernel or gitstore change), Security (no new trust boundary: the parent's cat-file takes a hex-only validated object id; no live service, CI or admin control touched) and Simplification.","body":{"conditions":"Independent review of exact head cbc3b81bd77424e6b141856264af7432c8a3c4f4 on request/scale-envelope-evidence (seventeen paths; two commits over main 9fbc913e: 0b689fe2 the harness head at which the campaign ran, then cbc3b81bd77424e6b141856264af7432c8a3c4f4 the pages and retained evidence; git merge-tree reports a clean merge onto current main), reporting artifact git:sha1:84ecd0f16c8efa6bb6abe3d106d348d2c4fd8549 (docs/reference/performance.md) and its sixteen exact-path companions, under request 0b5fdd93 (#20084) and promise 35715472. Report approved or changes-requested with gs review naming the reporting artifact first, recording Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions, and confirming from the retained files that every published number traces to a sample or evidence field and that no result is classified as a pass against an unadopted target.","no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0b5fdd93443cedeef9dbc4ddf733d8c0b0bdd60d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:84ecd0f16c8efa6bb6abe3d106d348d2c4fd8549 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:00925ae6c09fb0b8e2a72e84c22ca3488bc9534d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015aba51ab6c2416861618c5ac3c9ae0e444f17f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:063ac469f4327eef88a6cef497d6b24b5d128af7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:069ba281df08c36e7b19c66532ae24357887a9e5 and 97 more","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}